{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443186-cult-densities-in-cults-of-the-blood-gods","id":1443186,"title":"Cult densities in Cults of the Blood Gods","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-08T16:49:18-07:00","id":1443186,"title":"Cult densities in Cults of the Blood Gods","content":"So I am finalizing my Las Vegas Campaign I am preparing to run and I really like Cults of the Blood Gods. What I am trying to work out is how common these cults might be as a percentage of vampire population. Obviously the answer is whatever I feel like, but I want to get an idea of how other people see it.<br /> <br /> On Page 15 of Cults of the blood gods it suggests that in a city of millions there can be multiple faiths and sometimes multiple coteries of the same faith. So taking that logic to Las Vegas. I have a metropolitan population of about 3 million. I usually run a bit denser of a city and run one vampire for every 50k. About double the revised rule. That leaves me with sixty vampires. Assuming coteries of 5 ish members, 3 cults one with two coteries in that cult puts it at about 20 ish members of various cults. Thats about a third of the total population. Does that strike other storytellers as an accurate ratio of cult membership?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T16:55:35-07:00","id":1443187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443186-cult-densities-in-cults-of-the-blood-gods#post1443186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I am finalizing my Las Vegas Campaign I am preparing to run and I really like Cults of the Blood Gods. What I am trying to work out is how common these cults might be as a percentage of vampire population. Obviously the answer is whatever I feel like, but I want to get an idea of how other people see it.<br /> <br /> On Page 15 of Cults of the blood gods it suggests that in a city of millions there can be multiple faiths and sometimes multiple coteries of the same faith. So taking that logic to Las Vegas. I have a metropolitan population of about 3 million. I usually run a bit denser of a city and run one vampire for every 50k. About double the revised rule. That leaves me with sixty vampires. Assuming coteries of 5 ish members, 3 cults one with two coteries in that cult puts it at about 20 ish members of various cults. Thats about a third of the total population. Does that strike other storytellers as an accurate ratio of cult membership?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, my general impression of the cult densities for Kindred are that a typical cult in a city that is not actually run by said cult will be about 3-4 vampires. A &quot;cult&quot; in a Kindred city should probably be more equivalent to a coterie rather than an actual power in the city. Kindred are inherently suspicious after all and generally you're going to have a single priest or priestess prostetilyzing to either their childer or very close friends.<br /> <br /> For Las Vegas, I'd recommend going with the idea that it is a city of about fifty or sixty Kindred with it being compared to Chicago's 100 or so Kindred. There's always overpopulation in a tourist town, though so I wouldn't sweat too many details. However, I wouldn't be surprised if it's number of Blood Cultists is slightly higher than normal with the Ministry bound to be atracted to it.<br /> <br /> In my Las Vegas, I had the following Blood Cults:<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni: Obviously, they're doing their usual mobster thing.<br /> * The Church of Caine: A Mormon-influenced branch that was heavily into evangelizing and seemingly redemption for Kindred but actually preaching that being a vampire was a holy state not a damnation.<br /> * The Ministry: The Church of Set was very orthodox here and worked out of the Luxor for maximum irony. They were also being slowly pushed out by a group of Silent Striders murdering its members.<br /> * Church of Mithras: They hung out at Caesar's Palace because of course they did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-08-2021, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T17:07:27-07:00","id":1443189,"title":"","content":"That makes a lot of sense. I was actually leaning the same way. I lean towards a heavy Hecata population of Pisanob Giovanni and the Mexican one. Maybe 12-14 total. Add on 4 members of 3 cults and we have 24-25 ish. Thats a big chunk of the city so maybe I just build religiosity heavily into the theme of the town and story which seems appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T17:11:04-07:00","id":1443192,"title":"","content":"There's also the fact membership in a Blood Cult doesn't necessarily need to dominate a character's existence completely either. Dave the Sheriff might be a Cult of Mithras Knight but most days he's still an ex-heavyweight boxer and Camarilla loyalist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T20:38:10-07:00","id":1443209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443186-cult-densities-in-cults-of-the-blood-gods#post1443186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that strike other storytellers as an accurate ratio of cult membership?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel it is too high - it should probably be half that, with most vampires being indifferent and agnostic and just getting by night to night without faith of any kind guiding them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T04:30:20-07:00","id":1443239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443186-cult-densities-in-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1443209#post1443209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel it is too high - it should probably be half that, with most vampires being indifferent and agnostic and just getting by night to night without faith of any kind guiding them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that most agnostic kindred can be in a majority of mostly secular communities, with a minority of cities where cults are rampant. Then there can be others where they have simliar niches to the old independent clans (the same in Hecata's case) or Tremere chantries, albeit often with the overlap that CTPhipps described.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 04-09-2021, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T04:44:17-07:00","id":1443241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443186-cult-densities-in-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1443209#post1443209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel it is too high - it should probably be half that, with most vampires being indifferent and agnostic and just getting by night to night without faith of any kind guiding them.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a PC of mine once said, &quot;Vampires tend to be extremists in terms of religion. Becoming a literal walking corpse makes you believe either very strongly in God or not at all.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mind you, there's also a middle ground with Blood Cults as you don't have to be members of these crazy Kindred sects to have a religious bent.<br /> <br /> I also think that Kindred Society in V5 is getting something of a rise in believers due to the Ministry moving among them and the Camarilla no longer persecuting Cainite mythology. Previously, the vast majority of super-religious Cainites were restricted to the Sabbat and Gehenna Cults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}